{
  "id": "MO-SJR-2-2011",
  "scope": "state:mo",
  "title": "SJR 2 (2011 First Regular Session (96th General Assembly)): Allows enabling legislation for advance voting and photographic identification for voting",
  "urls": [
    "https://www.senate.mo.gov/11info/BTS_Web/Actions.aspx?SessionType=R&BillID=4065296",
    "https://www.senate.mo.gov/11info/pdf-bill/tat/SJR2.pdf",
    "https://www.senate.mo.gov/11info/pdf-bill/intro/SJR2.pdf",
    "https://www.senate.mo.gov/11info/pdf-bill/perf/SJR2.pdf",
    "https://www.senate.mo.gov/11info/pdf-bill/hcs/SJR2.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) SJR 2 (HCS#2) truly agreed text, proposed constitutional Section 9 proposed constitutional Section 9\n(quote) Section 9. A person seeking to vote in person in public elections may be required by general law to identify himself or herself and verify his or her qualifications as a citizen of the United States of America and a resident of the state of Missouri by providing election officials with a form of identification, which may include requiring valid government-issued photo identification. Exceptions to the identification requirement may also be provided for by general law.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) SJR 2 (HCS#2) truly agreed text, proposed constitutional Section 8, subsection 3 (advance voting)\n(quote) 3. If a voter identification requirement is provided by general law for in-person voting on election day, persons who desire to vote in advance of election day shall also comply with that identification requirement.\n(section) SJR 2 (HCS#2) truly agreed text, proposed constitutional Section 10 (absentee voting)\n(quote) Section 10. Different requirements for absentee voting when the voter does not appear before the election authority may be established by general law as may be necessary or desirable in order to accommodate the different purposes and administration requirements of this method of voting.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) SJR 2 (HCS#2) truly agreed text, Section B (official ballot title)\n(quote) Section B. The official ballot title for section A of this act shall read as follows: \"Shall the Missouri Constitution be amended to adopt the Voter Protection Act and allow the General Assembly to provide by general law for advance voting prior to election day, voter photo identification requirements, and voter requirements based on whether one appears to vote in person or by absentee ballot?\". T\n(other) Section 8 (HCS#2): advance in-person voting may be enabled by general law (third Saturday before election to first Tuesday before, excluding Sundays).\n(other) Section 10: different requirements for absentee voting may be set by general law.\n(other) Section 11: severability of sections 8, 9 and 10.",
  "sponsors": [
    {
      "name": "Stouffer",
      "role": "prime",
      "version": "HCS#2 SJR 2, truly agreed to and finally passed 5/9/2011 (LR 0282L.05T)"
    }
